1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://buhy.fr/decouvrir-buhy/un-peu-dhistoire/#mornay
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder [son of Françoise Crespin du Bec & Jacques de Mornay, Chevalier, Seigneur de Buhy] is '''M. Pierre de Mornay, Seigneur de Buhy, etc., who married Dame Anne d'Enlezy''', sole heiress of a good family in Bourbonnais, and w
2 CONC hose father owned a great deal of land in Normandy which she inherited. http://gw.geneanet.org/wailly?lang=en;p=jacques;n=de+mornay;oc=6
2 CONT
2 CONT ='[https://buhy.fr/decouvrir-buhy/patrimoine/chateau-de-buhy/'' Chateau de Buhy=  '']  (Click here !) 
2 CONT We should say the old castle, we have already mentioned this old heritage in the section on the Buhy farm and the agricultural activity which occupies the estate today.
2 CONT Pierre de Mornay had remodeled this magnificent 89-room castle with an equally magnificent wooded park. Today, along the RD14 before arriving at Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, you can still see on the left a long wall currently enclosing c
2 CONC ultivated land in the former castle park and a farmhouse with two square towers corresponding to the Renaissance dwellings, whose hidden doors and windows still allow you to imagine the building of that time. The semicircular wall
2 CONC  visible on maps of the time corresponded to the enclosure of the main courtyard of the Castle (still visible today).
2 CONT
2 CONT These are practically the only remains of the park and the outbuildings of the castle of Philippe Duplessis-Mornay. The only graphic testimony of the period and undoubtedly the most interesting is this engraving representing the c
2 CONC astle, but we believe that it is in fact only the "châtelet" which would be the entrance gate giving access to the main courtyard of the Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Remains of the main courtyard of the Château de Buhy
2 CONT Remains of the main courtyard of the Château de Buhy
2 CONT Engraving of the Châtelet de Buhy
2 CONT Engraving of the Châtelet de Buhy
2 CONT More precise than the maps of Cassini (César François Cassini de Thury 1714-1784) we can discover in the Atlas of Trudaine (Daniel-Charles de Trudaine 1703-1769) many very interesting details concerning the plan of the Château and
2 CONC  its environment, we also have an overview of what the Commune of Buhy and Buchet was with the communication routes lined with trees.
2 CONT
2 CONT Returning to the castle, we will particularly notice the imprint of the castle, the main courtyard, the imposing buildings surrounding the main courtyard and the numerous bridleways crisscrossing the park. The "monumental gate" in
2 CONC  perfect condition dating from 1779 allowed direct access from the park to the banks of the Cudron, as well as to the hill of the Bois d'Arnet via a tree-lined path.
