1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''General Comment'''
2 CONT
2 CONT This seems to be the furthest back we can thus far trace the origins of the Mendoza family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name itself could come from the either the location and/or the name of earlier ancestors.  There is a place in northern Spain called Mendoza.
2 CONT
2 CONT "de" can mean "of" or "from".  Many of the early Mendozas are recorded as "de or De Mendoza".   This could mean the family were originally "from Mendoza" and took this as their family name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another possibility is that the location was named after an individual named Mendoza which became the family name.  Son/Daughter "of/de Mendoza"
2 CONT
2 CONT Other comments and speculations welcome
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT he is my 9th great grandfather  I am Stephanie Shiller Mitchell born 1937 South Africa  now live in Cyprus
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
