1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Seigneur des Chauffours et de la Morandière, arrivé à Québec avec le gouverneur Lauzon en 1651, nommé major des troupes la mème année, membre du Conseil Souverain de Québec de 1663 à son décès, premier seigneur de 
2 CONC Matane. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Mathieu_D%27Amours&pid=830247&lng=fr&partID=830246
2 CONT
2 CONT http://tbasales.ipage.com/louviere/scroller_Louviere.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-LOUVIERE-DAMOUR.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathieu, son of Louis d'Amours, a conseiller du Roy, and Élisabeth Tessier of St.-Paul de Paris, was born in the French capital in c1618.  His family, a noble one, was well connected.  In October 1651, at age 33, Mathieu, still si
2 CONC ngle, arrived at Québec with the new Canadian governor, Lauzon.  Less than a year later, in April 1752 at Québec, Mathieu married Marie, daughter of Nicolas Marsolet de Saint-Aignan, a prominent Canadian.  In September 1663, at ag
2 CONC e 45, Mathieu became one of the seven founding members of the Conseil sourverain de Québec.  In November 1672, he obtained the seigneury of Matane.  He lived to a ripe old age, dying at Québec in October 1695, age 77.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathieu and Marie had 15 children, including nine sons, all born at Québec, seven of whom created families of their own.  At least five of Mathieu's sons also married into prominent Canadian families and received seigneuries like 
2 CONC their father:
2 CONT  Their children were: Nicolas, Joseph, Louis(1655) Mathieu(1657), Elisabeth(1658), Rene(1660), Charles(1662), Claude(1666), Bernard(1667), Genevieve(1673), Marie-Jacquette(1675), Marguerite(1677), Philippe(1680). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
