1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theresa Kunegunda Sobieska
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Theresa Kunegunda (Polish: Teresa Kunegunda Sobieska) (4 March 1676-10 March 1730) was a daughter of the Polish King John III Sobieski and Marie Casimire Louise de la Grange d'Arquien.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, the Kurfürst Maximilian II Emanuel, elector of Bavaria and married her on 2 January 1695 and she became the Bavarian Kurfürstin Therese Kunigunde.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was mother of ten children by her husband, including Karl VII, Holy Roman Emperor and Clemens August of Bavaria, Archbishop-Elector of Cologne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1704-05, in the ensuing evacuation of the Bavarian court to the Netherlands after the defeat in the Battle of Blenheim, she apparently was in charge of the government in Electoral Palatinate as Regent Princess Palatine.
2 CONT
2 CONT She rests in Theatinerkirche (Munich).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT A stillborn child (born and deceased in 1695)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna Karoline (1696-1750), became as nun om 29 October 1720 by the name "Therese Emanuele de corde Jesu" in Klarissinenkloster Munich
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl VII Albrecht (1697-1745), Holy Roman Emperor, King of Bohemia, and Elector of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Philipp Moritz Maria (1698-1719), posthumously elected bishop of Paderborn and bishop of Münster as news of his passing had not spread yet
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand Maria Innozenz (1699-1738), Imperial Fieldmarschall
2 CONT
2 CONT Clemens August (1700-1761), Archbishop of Cologne, Hoch- und Deutschmeister, Prince-Bishop of Hildesheim, Münster, Bishop of Paderborn and Osnabrück
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm (1701-1704), Prince of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Alois Johann Adolf (1702-1705), Prince of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Theodor of Bavaria (1703-1763), Cardinal, Prince-Bishop of Regensburg, Bishop of Freising and Bishop of Liège
2 CONT
2 CONT Maximilian Emanuel Thomas (1704-1709), Prince of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theresa_Kunegunda_Sobieska
2 CONT
