1 NOTE {geni:about_me} •The progenitor of the Dutch branch of the Mendoza family, David de Mendoza, is believed to have come from Seville where his wife Abigail de la Penha Castro was born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT David Mendoza: "Where to start? He is reportedly born in Jaen in 1655, not Seville. All his reported siblings are unknown. He had a brother in Amsterdam records as David de Castro. Samson was a nephew. On my phone so don't have a 
2 CONC London death date to hand. No evidence his parents were Mendozas...   Of course, we Mendozas are really Castros"
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Was a Master of Arms Life significantly affected by Spanish Inquisition Ultimately escaped to Amsterdam and then moved to London Story is covered by Mark Wright "Who do you think you are?" UK edition 2019
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-497724231-1-500073/david-antonio-de-mendoza-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-a55a6f14399115650f080b93521083c1&mrid=97fdd338530b75716704a5f9dbcd5a46 MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 2 2021, 9:56:48 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
