1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LXP4-R4L
2 CONT Brief Life History of Charles'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Charles Cassé was born on 29 March 1682, in Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France, his father, Antoine Cassé, was 40 and his mother, Françoise De Pitié, was 47. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Françoise Paquier (1682-1731) on 12 September 1703, in Saint-Étienne-de-Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 9 daughters. 
2 CONT Infant male Lacasse 1704–1704
2 CONT Infant female Cassé 1704–1704
2 CONT Marie Francoise Casse 1705–1754
2 CONT Antoine Lacasse 1707–1768
2 CONT Marie Josèphe Lacasse 1709–1761
2 CONT Charles Cassé 1711–1730
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Lacasse 1713–1792
2 CONT Marie Marguerite Casse 1715–1750
2 CONT Marguerite Lacasse 1715–1750
2 CONT Marie Madeleine Cassé 1716–1786
2 CONT Marie Lacasse 1717–
2 CONT Marie "Charlotte" Cassé 1718–1788
2 CONT Marie "Angélique" Cassé 1720–1738
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd wife Marie Josèphe Filteau (1705–1781)
2 CONT on 19 octobre 1734 in Saint-Vallier, Bellechasse, Québec, Canada
2 CONT They had at least 5 children:
2 CONT Charles Cassé Lacase 1736–1814
2 CONT Marie "Marthe" Cassé 1738–1760
2 CONT Ignace LaCasse 1740–1766
2 CONT Marie "Louise" LaCasse 1742–1777
2 CONT Joseph-Marie LaCasse 1744–1815
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 27 November 1749, in Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France, at the age of 67, and was buried in Saint-Étienne-de-Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France.
2 CONT
2 CONT
