1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.100megsfree2.com/jjscherr/jacques/descendantslouisvii.htm Click Here!
2 CONT
2 CONT Fully Featured Website Hosting!!! The Royal Descent  of the Mayotte (Maillot, Mailhot) Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor (Aliénor) of Aquitaine &  LouisVII, "The Younger" Capet, King of France
2 CONT
2 CONT and Forward to the Present
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. I
2 CONT
2 CONT  1. Louis1 Vll, "The Younger" Capet, King of France was born 1120, and died September 18, 1180 in Paris, France. He married (1) Eleanor-Aliénor d'Aquitaine July 22, 1137 in Bordeaux Cathedral, Bordeaux, France, daughter of William
2 CONC  X and Eleanor Chatet de Rochefoucauldlleraul She was born 1122 in Chateau de Belin, Guinne, France, and died March 31, 1204 in Fontevraud Abbey, Maine-et-Loire, France. He married (2) Constanza Alfonsez, Princess of Castile 1154 
2 CONC in Castile, Spain She was born Abt. 1140. He married (3) Adele (Alix) Countess of Champagne November 07, 1160. She was born Abt. 1140
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis VII surrounded by bishops and courtiers.  (BNF, FR 2813) fol. 211  Grandes Chroniques de France  France, Paris, 14th Century.  (70 x 65 mm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for LouisVII, "The Younger" Capet, King of France: (died at age 60):
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis was of the 3rd Frankish dynasty (Capetian) which ruled in a direct line from 897 to 1328 starting with Hugh Capet. and then through collateral lines from then until the French Revolution through the branches of Valois and Bo
2 CONC urban.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Eleanor-Alienor d'Aquitaine:
2 CONT
2 CONT Aliénor (Eleonore) was directly descended from Charlemagne Aliénor, (Eleonore) died at the age of 82. She was the first of three wives of Louis VII. She was Duchess of d'Aquitaine - de Gascogne and Countess of de Poitiers. 1137-12
2 CONC 04 Countess of Saintonge, Angoumois, Limousin, Auvergne, Bordeaux, Agen.
2 CONT
