1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sources=
2 CONT * Location info: [http://www.geni.com/projects/Qu%C3%A9bec-Qu%C3%A9bec-Canada/23941 Québec]
2 CONT * [http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?pid=24217 NosOrigines.qc.ca ID No: 24217]
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ren%C3%A9-Louis_Chartier_de_Lotbini%C3%A8re Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT René-Louis Chartier de Lotbinière (1641–1709) was a French-Canadian Poet, 1st Seigneur de Lotbinière in New France (1672), Judge of the Provost and Admiralty Courts and Chief Councillor of the Sovereign Council of New France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptised 14 November 1641, in the Church of Saint-Nicholas-des-Champs in Paris, he was the son of Louis-Théandre Chartier de Lotbinière and Élisabeth d'Amours de Clignancourt (1613–1690), daughter of Louis d'Amours de Louvieres (d
2 CONC ied 1640), Sieur de Serain, Chief Councillor to King Henry IV of France at the Grand Châtelet, Paris. He was the brother-in-law of Philippe de Rigaud Vaudreuil, Governor General of New France, and the uncle of the last Governor Ge
2 CONC neral of New France, Pierre François de Rigaud, Marquis de Vaudreuil-Cavagnal. He was the grandfather of Michel Chartier de Lotbinière, Marquis de Lotbinière and Nicolas Renaud d'Avene des Meloizes, Marquis de Fresnoy. In 1651, at
2 CONC  the age of ten, he arrived with his parents in New France, and was educated there at the Jesuit's College in Quebec City.
