1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_Maria_Innozenz_von_Bayern de.wikipedia.org...] ; [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_Maria_Innocenz_of_Bavaria en.wikipedia.org...] ; [http://gw1.geneanet.org/hwember1?
2 CONC lang=de&m=NG&n=Ferdinand%22_1699+von+Bayern&t=PN gw1.geneanet.org...] ; 
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT * Ferdinand Maria Innocent was a son of Elector Maximilian II Emanuel of Bavaria (1662-1726) from his marriage to Therese Kunigunde Sobieska (1676-1730 ), a daughter of King John III Sobieski of Poland.
2 CONT * He served as a general in the imperial army. In 1738, he was promoted to Field marshal and imperial Feldzeugmeister[1].
2 CONT * He died in 1738 and was buried in the Theatine Church in Munich.
2 CONT ===Marriage and issue===
2 CONT * Ferdinand Maria Innocent married on 5 February 1719 in Zákupy to Maria Anna Carolina, a daughter of Philip William August, Count Palatine of Neuburg. He had the following children:
2 CONT >* Maximilian Francis Joseph (1720-1738)
2 CONT >* Clement Francis de Paula (1722-1770); married in 1742 Countess Palatine Maria Anna of Sulzbach (1722-1790)
2 CONT >* Therese Emmanuel (1723-1743)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ferdinand also had a son from his extra-marital affaire with Countess Marie Adelaide Fortunata Spaur (1694-1781):
2 CONT >* Joseph Ferdinand (1718-1805), Duke of Salern, married: in 1753 to Countess Marie Mechthildis of Törring (1734-1764); in 1766 to Countess Josepha of La Rosee (d. 1772)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * [http://gw1.geneanet.org/hwember1?lang=en;pz=maximilian;nz=von+bayern;ocz=10;p=ferdinand;n=von+bayern '''Ferdinand von Bayern''']
