1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel. ''' ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700''''', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966
2 CONC , pages 100-101, #348 [IV, fol. 110 v., no. 48].  ...  This protocolo is the '''will of Captain Pedro de la Garza''', born in Nuevo Leon and the '''son of Captain Pedro de la Garza and Inés Rodríguez''', both deceased.  He states 
2 CONC that he wishes to be buried in the Parrish Church and that he is '''married to María de la Rocha''' who had no dowry.  Their '''children are José (deceased), Pedro, María, Juana, Lucía, Nicolasa, Inés, Antonia, Francisco, and Juan
2 CONC '''.  He names his children's spouses and sets forth his debts and his bequests.  Dated '''19 October 1688, Hacienda of Saint Nicolas, jurisdiction of Monterrey'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''______________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro De La Garza Falcon,The Younger 
2 CONT *(son of Pedro De La Garza Falcon and Ines Rodriguez) was born Bet. 1612 - 1615 in Nuevo Reino de Leon,Mexico, and 
2 CONT *died 20 Nov 1695 in Monterrey,Nuevo Leon,Mexico. 
2 CONT *He married Maria De La Roche
2 CONT
2 CONT .http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/a/b/o/Dorothy-M-Aboyte/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0214.html
2 CONT
2 CONT '''______________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT This is on the descendants of The Descendents of Captain Pedro de la Garza  
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. CAPTAIN PEDRO3 DE-LA-GARZA-RODRIGUEZ (PEDRO2 DE-LA-GARZA-FALCON-TREVINO, MARCOS-ALONSO1 DE-LA-GARZA-Y-ARCON) was born Abt. 1613 in Nuevo Leon, Mexico, and died 20 Nov 1695 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico. He married MARIA-LUCI
2 CONC A ROBLES-Y-DE-LA-ROCHA Bet. 1635 - 1644 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, daughter of JUAN DE-LA-ROCHA and JUANA ROBLES. She was born 1630 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, and died 1675 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPTAIN PEDRO DE-LA-GARZA-RODRIGUEZ:
2 CONT
2 CONT He Signed his last will and testament on October 19, 1688. Source: Origin of the Surnames Garza and Trevino by Tomas Mendirichaga Cueva. Page 14.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of PEDRO DE-LA-GARZA-RODRIGUEZ and MARIA-LUCIA ROBLES-Y-DE-LA-ROCHA are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. i. JOSEPH4 DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, d. Bef. 20 Nov 1695, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19. ii. LUCIA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, d. 29 Aug 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20. iii. MARIANNA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, d. 08 Jun 1717, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT 21. iv. JUAN PEREZ-DE-LA-GARZA, b. Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico; d. 16 Mar 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT 22. v. MARIA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 23. vi. ALFEREZ FRANCISCO DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, d. Montemorelos, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. vii. ANTONIA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 25. viii. CAPTAIN PEDRO DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, b. Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT 26. ix. NICOLASA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, b. 1648.
2 CONT
2 CONT 27. x. JUANA DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, b. 1652.
2 CONT
2 CONT 28. xi. MARIA-INEZ DE-LA-GARZA-DE-LA-ROCHA, b. 1653, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/garza.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''______________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro the younger was born in Nuevo Leon between 1612 and 161i5. Between 1642 and 1676 served as alderman, procurer, and assistant mayor (1659 and 1683) of Monterrey. His hacienda was Hacienda de San Nicolas, now called San Nicola
2 CONC s de los Garzas. Awarded an encomienda in 1663. It is said of him "Pedro de la Garza, resident of this kingdom, who is a meritorious person and the son of a conquistador; and who has served His Majesty with full approbation, in al
2 CONC l the occasions that have offered themselves to be in the royal service as a good soldier and as his loyal vassal." In 1691, the governor of Nuevo Leon made reference to him "as a meritorious peron, old, and citizen of the said ki
2 CONC ngdom, and that since his first years, he has served His Majesty in it with very well known merits, risking his person on different occasions against the Indians rebelling against the crown." (Mendirichaga 1989,14)  My direct ance
2 CONC stor, Ines de la Garza, his daughter, would marry Jose Martinez, the founder of San Antonio de los Martinez, later the villa of Marin. Ref: "Conquistadores and Crypto-Jews of Monterrey" David T. Raphael (c. 2001)
2 CONT --------------------
