1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LDF9-VLQ
2 CONT Brief Life History of Marguerite'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Marguerite Cassé was born on 12 December 1711, in Saint-Étienne-de-Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France, her father, Joseph Cassé, was 42 and her mother, Marie Bazin, was 38. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Pierre Louis Gontier (1711-1756) on 11 August 1734, in Saint-Étienne-de-Beaumont, Québec, Canada, New France. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 7 daughters. 
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Gontier 1735–1735
2 CONT Pierre Gontier 1737–
2 CONT Marguerite Gonthier 1739–1809
2 CONT Louis Gontier 1741–
2 CONT Marie Genevieve Gontier 1744–1744
2 CONT Marie Ursule Gontier 1746–
2 CONT Marie Josephe Gontier 1748–1828
2 CONT JEAN FRANCOIS GONTIER 1750–1750
2 CONT Marguerite Goutier 1752–
2 CONT Marie Angélique Gonthier 1754–1835
2 CONT Marie Catherine Gontier 1756–1830
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her 1st husband, she married 2nd husband Joseph Athanase Beaudoin (1705–1783)
2 CONT on 14 février 1763 in Saint-Charles-de-Bellechasse, Bellechasse, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT No children on record.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 20 May 1788, in Saint-Charles-Borromée, Berthier, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 76, and was buried in Saint-Charles-Borromée, Berthier, Quebec, Canada.
