1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vicente Ferrer Chapa (0360) is the illegitimate son of Juana de Chapa (0205). Mendirichaga Cueva in his book, Apellidos de Nuevo Leon - Siglo XVI, XVII y XVIII, page 108, states that "Maria Josefa Chapa, legitimate
2 CONC  daughter of Vicente Chapa and Maria de Torres, married on 20 April 1735, Francisco Xavier Perez, the legitimate son of Juan Perez and Manuela Garcia.
2 CONT
2 CONT To support the conclusion that this Vicente Chapa is the son of Juana de Chapa, assume that people, generally, marry around age 20 and start having their families. Vicente would have been approximately 40 when his daughter married
2 CONC  (20 years for Vicente to marry plus 20 years for his daughter). Under this assumption, Vicente would have been born (1735 - 40 = 1695) arround 1695. From a time standpoint, Juana de Chapa must be the mother. There were only two C
2 CONC hapa women of childbearing age at that time - Maria and Juana de Chapa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Josefa Chapa (0472), daughter of Vicente Chapa (0360) and Maria de Torres married Francisco Xavier Perez, son of Juan Perez and Manuela Garcia on 20 April 1735.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
