1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Juan Bautista Chapa (0203) was born circa 1657 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, the legitimate son of Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) and Beatriz Olivares de Trevino. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is known to have been in the military, resided in Villaldama around 1700, and was the mayor of Villaldama in 1705. He filed his Last Will and Testament in November 1709 and died after 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Quinones of San Antonio, Texas, researched the padrinos (godparents) named in a Monterrey baptismal record for Juan Joseph Chapa dated March 24, 1710. Padrino Pedro Regalado Trevino, who became a priest, was the son of Mari
2 CONC a de Chapa (0204) and the baby's first cousin. For this relationship to be true, the baby's father Juan de Chapa, must be a sibling to Maria de Chapa (0204); hence, Juan de Chapa and Juan Bautista Chapa (0203) are the same person.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Given this relationship the followng records are found in the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon.
2 CONT *Juan de Chapa (0203) married Maria de Munguia on July 27, 1695, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. [M601491-0321] They had the following son:
2 CONT *Juan Joseph Chapa Munguia (0340) who was born March 24, 1710. [M601491-2104]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
