1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 6. Juana Chapa (0205) is one about whom not much is known. Juana is reported to have died on November 8, 1709, in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. In her Testament she declared that she had three children out of wedlock
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana Chapa (0205) was the legitimate daughter of Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) and Beatriz Olivares de Trevino. Juana never married, however, in her testament, dated November 6, 1709, she "...declared as her illegitimate children Cr
2 CONC istóbal, now dead, Vicente Ferrer and María Josefa, to whom she left and named as heirs". Juana was buried in Monterrey on November 8, 1709. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana Chapa (0205) had the following children out of wedlock:
2 CONT *1. Vicente Ferrer Chapa (0360) born ca 1695.
2 CONT *2. Cristobal Chapa (0361) died before 1709.
2 CONT *3. Maria Josepha Chapa (0362) born ca 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Mendirichaga Cueva, Tomas, Apellidos de Nuevo Leon - Siglos XVI, XVII y XVIII, Groupo Financiero Banorte, 1993, p-107.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reference cited for the above declaration by Juana de Chapa is the same document abstracted in the Catalogo y Sintesis de los Protocolos Archivo Municipal de Monterrey, Vol 2, page 104, entry 1175. The problem is that Mendrich
2 CONC aga read the original document with "Juana de Chapa" while the Protocolos abstract records it as "Juan de Chapa". Only a rereading of the original document will determine the true parentage. I have written Israel Cavazos Garza to 
2 CONC have the original reread. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPA - CHAPTER 4 Re: José Matías Longoria-Camargo/Matamoros Branch 
2 CONT *Posted by: Loretta Garcia (ID *****8749) Date: December 13, 2005 at 12:15:09 
2 CONT *In Reply to: José Matías Longoria-Camargo/Matamoros Branch by Lino GarciaJr  of 1155  
2 CONT *Chapa: The First Four Generations
2 CONT
2 CONT JUAN BAUTISTA SCHIAPAPRIA (CHAPA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Schiapapria (0100) was born in Villa Albisola on the coast of Italy and was baptized on November 16, 1627, the legitimate son of Bartholome Schiapapria and Batistina Badi. He left Italy in 1647 for New Spain. He marr
2 CONC ied Beatriz Olivares de Trevino in 1653. Beatriz was the legitimate daughter of Juan Olivares and Juana de Trevino.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) was a conquistador, discoverer, and author. He served as secretary to the governors of Nuevo Leon and Coahuila. He died April 20, 1695, at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *1. Juan Bautista Chapa (0203), the younger, was born circa 1657 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, resided in Villaldama around 1700, was mayor of Villaldama in 1705, and also is believed to be known as Juan de Chapa. Juan (Bautista) de Ch
2 CONC apa married Maria de Munguia on July 27, 1695, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon (M601491-0321). They had one son from this union.
2 CONT *2. Nicolas Chapa (0206) was born 1655 and married Ines Benavides Flores in 1710 and had six children.
2 CONT *3. Gaspar Chapa (0202) died on January 8, 1694. He never married but lived in common law with Maria Gonzalez and they had at least one child.
2 CONT *4. Jose Maria Chapa (0200) was born circa 1663. He married Nicolasa Fernandez in 1694. On September 12, 1697, he married Josefa Sanchez de la Barrera. From his second marriage he had two children. He married Maria Francisca de Oc
2 CONC hoa on June 27, 1717 at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon [M601497-0767]. There was one child from the third marriage.
2 CONT *5. Maria Chapa (0204) married Alferez Real Francisco de Trevino. They had four children. Maria died before 1709.
2 CONT *6. '''Juana Chapa''' (0205) is one about whom not much is known. Juana is reported to have died on November 8, 1709, in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. In her Testament she declared that she had three children out of wedlock.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT -------------------- MARIA CHAPA
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Chapa (0204) is the legitimate daughter of Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) and Beatriz Olivares de Trevino. Maria married Royal Lieutenant Francisco de Trevino, the son of Captain Alejo de Trevino and Maria de Arriola. (1) Maria 
2 CONC Chapa died by 1709.
2 CONT *1. Francisco Trevino (0310) married Clara Josefa de Cepeda. (Clara Saens). Marriage Investigations, #62-2, April 25, 1701.
2 CONT *2. Josefa Trevino (0311) married Bernabe Villarreal. Marriage Investigations, #62-24, January 2, 1702. Josepha de Trevino (0314) married Julio de la Mancha. Marriage Investigations #45-9, February 11, 1707.
2 CONT *3. Maria Rosa Trevino (0312) married Francisco Nunez de Carvajal. Marriage Investigations, #62-19, June 21, 1701.
2 CONT *4. Pedro Regalado de Trevino (0313). Became a Priest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Analysis of the avaliable records suggest that Francisco de Trevino died shortly after 1694 and that Maria remarried around 1695+ to Francisco Narcisco de la Garza. The Catalogo y Sintesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal d
2 CONC e Monterrey, 1875) XIII, fol. 196, no. 86, indicates that there were only two children by this marriage and that "... when his parents died [Maria de Chapa and Francisco Narcisco de la Garza], he was left under the care of Nicolas
2 CONC  de Chapa ..." some time around 1709. Nicolas de Chapa is a brother of Maria de Chapa and lived in Cerralvo so it would be natural for him to take his sister's son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: (1) Mendirichaga Cueva, Tomas, Apellidos de Nuevo Leon - Siglos XVI, XVII y XVIII, Groupo Financiero Banorte, 1993, p 106-107.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
