1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nicolas CHAPA[434],[898] 
2 CONT *was born on 1 January 1670 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, New Spain.[430] 
2 CONT *He died before 24 May 1735 at the age of 65 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, New Spain. 
2 CONT *He founded General Treviño, in Nuevo Leon, naming it after the patriarch of his mother's family. 
2 CONT *Parents: Juan Bautista CHAPA and Beatrice OLIVARES de Treviño.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Ynes BAEZ DE BENAVIDES. 
2 CONT *Ynes BAEZ DE BENAVIDES and Nicolas CHAPA were married in 1700 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, New Spain.[430] 
2 CONT *Children were: 
2 CONT **1. Maria Clara de CHAPA, 
2 CONT **2. Ynes CHAPA, 
2 CONT **3. Antonia CHAPA, 
2 CONT **4. Miguel Eusebio CHAPA, 
2 CONT **5. Juan Bautista CHAPA, 
2 CONT **6. Maria CHAPA Benavides, 
2 CONT **7. Jose Florencio CHAPA.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b42.html#P910
2 CONT
2 CONT ========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Schiapapria Chapa
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 1
2 CONT *1. Juan Bautista Schiapapria1 Chapa 
2 CONT **was born Abt 1624 in Albísola, Italy, and 
2 CONT **died Abt 1694 in Monterrey. 
2 CONT **He married Beatris Treviño Abt 1652 in Monterrey, daughter of Juan de Olivares and Juana de Treviño.
2 CONT **Children of Juan Chapa and Beatris Treviño are:
2 CONT ***2 i. Gaspar Treviño2 Chapa, born Abt 1654 in Monterrey. 
2 CONT ***3 ii. José Maria Treviño Chapa, born Abt 1655 in Monterrey.
2 CONT ***+ 4 iii. Nicolas Chapa Treviño, born Abt 1655 in Monterrey. 
2 CONT ***5 iv. Maria Treviño Chapa, born Abt 1656 in Monterrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 2
2 CONT *4. Nicolas2 Chapa Treviño (Juan Bautista Schiapapria1 Chapa) 
2 CONT **was born Abt 1655 in Monterrey, . 
2 CONT **He married Inez Benavides Báez Flores Abt 1675 in Monterrey, daughter of Francisco Benavides Martinez and Clara de la Cerda.
2 CONT **Children of Nicolas Chapa Treviño and Inez Benavides Báez Flores are:
2 CONT ***+ 6 i. Maria3 Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1698 in Monterrey.
2 CONT ***+ 7 ii. Clara Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1700 in Cerralvo; died in Cerralvo.
2 CONT ***+ 8 iii. Ines Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1701 in Cerralvo .
2 CONT ***+ 9 iv. Miguel Eusebio Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1705 in Monterrey.
2 CONT ***10 v. Antonia Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1713 in Monterrey .
2 CONT ***11 vi. Florencio Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1770 in Monterrey . 
2 CONT ***12 vii. Juan Bautista Chapa Benavides, born Abt 1771 in Monterrey .
2 CONT
2 CONT http://longoriaf.tripod.com/Chapa.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolas Chapa (0206) 
2 CONT *was born in 1655 the legitimate son of Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) and Beatriz Olivares de Trevino. 
2 CONT *Nicolas married Ines Benavides Flores, the daughter of Captain Francisco de Benavides and Clara Flores, in 1710 and had six children.
2 CONT **1. Jose Florencio Chapa (0320) was born circa 1714. He married Margarita de la Pena and they had nine children.
2 CONT **2. Maria Ines Chapa (0324) first married Juan Antonio Ruiz Garza. Her second marriage was to Manuel de Hinojosa. There were four children from the second marriage.
2 CONT **3. Antonia Chapa (0325) married Jose Salinas.
2 CONT **4. Clara Maria Chapa (0326) also known as Maria Chapa married Jose Diego de Longoria. They had nine children.
2 CONT **5. Miguel Eusebio Chapa (0327) married Ana Maria Garcia. They had two children.
2 CONT **6. Juan Bautista Chapa (0321) married Rita Lopez de Jean. They had five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Nicolas, Juan Bautista, and Jose Maria had sixteen years of military by 1688 to support their claim to a Royal Grant of Land. They duly received the grants in the neighborhood of Paras, Agualeguas and General Trevino. Nicolas mar
2 CONC ried Ines Benavides Flores in 1710 and founded General Trevino which he named after the founder of his mother's family in Nuevo Leon."
2 CONT
2 CONT Duaine, Carl L., Caverns of Oblivion, Packrat Press, Manchaca, Texas, 1971, page 140. It is possible that Nicolas Chapa (0206) second marriage was to Maria de Romero. The birth of a daughter, Maria Gertrudis Chapa is recorded for 
2 CONC 1738 in the Monterrey Microfilm Records 8029660- 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
